Package: totaljs-services
Version: 1.0.0-1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Total.js <repository@totaljs.com>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: totaljs-docker-stack (>= 1.0.0)
Homepage: https://www.totaljs.com
Description: Optional services for Total.js developers: Redis, Mailpit, MongoDB
 A small catalog of services that run as Docker containers on the network of the
 Total.js Developer Distros, and are off until the person turns them on with the
 command totaljs-service (list, enable, disable, status). Each one is a Compose
 file in /www/services/<name> that the person can edit, and a systemd service
 (totaljs-service@<name>) that starts at boot and tries again until the images
 are downloaded. None of them is published on the host: the projects reach them
 by name (redis, mailpit, mongodb) through the network proxy.
